---
// Where OpenIVM hooks into DuckDB (after Figures 1–2 of the SIGMOD 2024 demo paper).
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <div class="scroll">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 1040 340" role="img" aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc">
      <title id="arch-title">OpenIVM inside DuckDB</title>
      <desc id="arch-desc">
        A CREATE MATERIALIZED VIEW statement enters DuckDB's parser. OpenIVM's fallback parser strips the
        materialized-view options and stores metadata. After planning, OpenIVM's optimizer rules rebind scans to delta
        tables and apply delta rules. The incremental plan either runs natively in DuckDB or is compiled back to SQL for
        other engines such as PostgreSQL or Spark.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="arch-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M0 0 10 5 0 10z" class="head"></path>
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- lanes -->
      <rect class="lane" x="210" y="16" width="590" height="124" rx="16"></rect>
      <text class="lane-label" x="230" y="42">DuckDB</text>
      <rect class="lane ext" x="210" y="176" width="820" height="148" rx="16"></rect>
      <text class="lane-label ext" x="230" y="202">OpenIVM extension</text>

      <!-- input -->
      <rect class="box input" x="12" y="58" width="168" height="58" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="mono" x="26" y="82">CREATE MATERIALIZED</text>
      <text class="mono" x="26" y="100">VIEW regional_totals …</text>

      <!-- DuckDB core -->
      <g class="core">
        <rect class="box" x="236" y="62" width="120" height="50" rx="10"></rect>
        <text class="t" x="296" y="92">parser</text>
        <rect class="box" x="376" y="62" width="120" height="50" rx="10"></rect>
        <text class="t" x="436" y="92">planner</text>
        <rect class="box" x="516" y="62" width="120" height="50" rx="10"></rect>
        <text class="t" x="576" y="92">optimizer</text>
        <rect class="box" x="656" y="62" width="120" height="50" rx="10"></rect>
        <text class="t" x="716" y="92">executor</text>
      </g>

      <!-- extension -->
      <rect class="box ivm" x="226" y="218" width="160" height="84" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="306" y="244">fallback parser</text>
      <text class="s" x="306" y="266">strips MV options,</text>
      <text class="s" x="306" y="282">stores view metadata</text>

      <rect class="box ivm" x="496" y="218" width="160" height="84" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="576" y="244">IVM optimizer rules</text>
      <text class="s" x="576" y="266">delta model, lineage,</text>
      <text class="s" x="576" y="282">operator rewriting</text>

      <rect class="box ivm" x="760" y="218" width="170" height="84" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="845" y="244">LPTS</text>
      <text class="s" x="845" y="266">plan → AST → CTEs</text>
      <text class="s" x="845" y="282">→ target dialect</text>

      <!-- targets -->
      <rect class="box target" x="836" y="40" width="186" height="96" rx="10"></rect>
      <text class="t" x="929" y="66">refresh SQL</text>
      <text class="s" x="929" y="88">DuckDB · PostgreSQL</text>
      <text class="s" x="929" y="106">Spark (soon) · …</text>

      <!-- flow -->
      <g class="flow">
        <path d="M180 87H232" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M356 87H372" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M496 87H512" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M636 87H652" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M776 87H832" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M656 260H756" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M929 214V140" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
      </g>
      <g class="flow hook">
        <path d="M282 112V214" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M330 214V116" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M552 112V214" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
        <path d="M600 214V116" marker-end="url(#arch-arrow)"></path>
      </g>
      <text class="lbl" x="276" y="160" text-anchor="end">MV keywords</text>
      <text class="lbl" x="336" y="160">clean SQL</text>
      <text class="lbl" x="546" y="160" text-anchor="end">logical plan</text>
      <text class="lbl" x="606" y="160">incremental plan</text>
      <text class="lbl" x="804" y="78" text-anchor="middle">native</text>
      <text class="lbl" x="706" y="252" text-anchor="middle">plan</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    OpenIVM is a DuckDB extension: it plugs into the parser and the optimizer without modifying the core engine,
    then compiles the incremental plan back to SQL through LPTS. Adapted from the SIGMOD 2024 demo paper.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .diagram {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 760px;
    height: auto;
  }
  .lane {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 60%, transparent);
    stroke: var(--border);
  }
  .lane.ext {
    stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--insert) 35%, transparent);
    stroke-dasharray: 5 5;
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--insert) 4%, transparent);
  }
  .lane-label {
    font: 600 13px var(--font-mono);
    fill: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  }
  .lane-label.ext {
    fill: var(--insert);
  }
  .box {
    fill: var(--surface-2);
    stroke: var(--border-strong);
  }
  .box.ivm {
    stroke: var(--insert);
  }
  .box.target {
    stroke: var(--accent);
  }
  .box.input {
    fill: var(--bg);
  }
  .t {
    font: 600 13px var(--font-mono);
    fill: var(--text);
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .s {
    font: 400 11.5px var(--font-mono);
    fill: var(--muted);
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .mono {
    font: 500 11.5px var(--font-mono);
    fill: var(--accent);
  }
  .flow path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--faint);
    stroke-width: 1.6;
  }
  .flow.hook path {
    stroke: var(--insert);
    stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
  }
  .head {
    fill: var(--faint);
  }
  .lbl {
    font: 400 11px var(--font-mono);
    fill: var(--faint);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: var(--faint);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    max-width: 90ch;
  }
</style>
